.TH tubase32 n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tubase32
.PP
RFC 4648 base32 (and base32hex) encode/decode in pure Tcl. Tcl core provides base64 but not base32, so this fills the gap with a matching API.
.SS API
.CS
set b32  [::tclutils::tubase32::encode $bytes]
set data [::tclutils::tubase32::decode $b32]
.CE
.PP
Commands:
.IP \(bu
\fBencode data ?\-pad bool? ?\-hex bool?\fR — base32 string. \fB\-pad 0\fR omits the trailing \fB=\fR; \fB\-hex 1\fR uses the base32hex alphabet (RFC 4648 §7). Default \fB\-pad 1 \-hex 0\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBdecode text ?\-hex bool?\fR — back to a binary string. Whitespace and \fB=\fR padding are ignored; input is case\-insensitive.
.IP \(bu
\fBencodeFile path ?\-pad bool? ?\-hex bool?\fR — encode a file's bytes.
.IP \(bu
\fBdecodeFile path ?\-hex bool?\fR — decode a file's text.
.PP
Errors use error code \fB{TCLUTILS TUBASE32 CHAR}\fR for an invalid input character.
